2026-09-27T07:22:16.3571752Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3572859Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3573551Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3575347Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3577296Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3577549Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3578109Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3578795Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3579436Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3579712Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3580261Z ================
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3580539Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3580942Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3581836Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3582337Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3582730Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3583444Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3583866Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3584156Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3585111Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3585983Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3587473Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3588618Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3588978Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3589929Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3591094Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3591847Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3593426Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3594386Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3594834Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3595341Z ========
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3595585Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3598427Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3601509Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3602005Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3603294Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3604936Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3606460Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3607702Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3608829Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3609452Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3609865Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3610815Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3611164Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3612729Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3614199Z 
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3615059Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3616326Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:22:16.3616660Z 
